WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:00.867
Carson, who was at the

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.702
Capitol that day, as you know,

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.704
was your vice president, Mike Pence,

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.773
who says that you endangered his life

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:07.941
on that day.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:09.442
I don't think he was in any danger.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:09.676
Mr.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.410
President,

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.512
do you feel that you owe him an apology?

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.347
No, because he did something wrong.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.682
He should have put the votes back

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.117
to the state legislatures.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:17.884
And I think we would have

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:20.820
had a different outcome. I really do.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.022
And he doesn't have the authority

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.758
to do that. As you know what,

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:25.658
the vice president does

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.894
not have the authority to reject

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:28.495
this election,

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.096
not just now, because it's interesting.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.332
Let's keep it interesting. Right.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:33.600
I like Mike Pence very much.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.501
He's a very fine man.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.502
He's a very nice man.

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:36.369
He made a mistake.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:39.072
His lawyer said you cannot move.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.007
I call them the human conveyor belt.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:41.374
I said,

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.742
even if the votes you mean

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.376
talk to us, like

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.110
even if the votes

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.212
are absolutely fraudulent, he can't.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:46.679
Yes, sir.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:47.580
He can't even read.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.848
And the Democrats played it

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.550
and the rhinos played it.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.585
And then the election was over.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.620
They told him he couldn't do it.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.854
And Mike said to me, I can't do it.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:55.922
The lawyers told me, you can't do it.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:56.956
They can't do it.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.224
But the lawyers are wrong.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.393
Because right after the election,

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.694
they all met the rhinos

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:02.862
and the Democrats,

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.397
and they worked out a plan

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.765
to make sure that future

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:06.666
vice presidents

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:09.269
don't do what I said you could do.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.070
That's not what happened.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.805
You're referring to the electoral count.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.540
I've read I've read that there is

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.607
there is no authority.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.408
Legal experts,

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.110
including Republican legal experts,

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.111
say that he does not

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.279
have that authority, persuasion.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.347
But why did they change the law then,

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.549
saying that you can't do it?

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.483
They didn't change the law.

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.284
They strengthened the law

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.251
because they were worried about

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.920
the strength it you could do

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.189
It's not what it means.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.123
Thank you.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.758
They strengthened my card,

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.226
the right to do it.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.695
They convinced him he didn't.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:36.763
And it was a horrible thing.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.664
For our country.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.065
If you would have sent those votes

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:41.101
back to Georgia, Pennsylvania

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.735
and other states, Wisconsin,

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.337
which if you look at Wisconsin,

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.572
they've virtually admitted

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.574
now that the election was rigged.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.375
If they would have sent those votes back

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.144
to many of those states,

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:52.846
they would not come back

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.013
in the affirmative.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.915
And remember what I said

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.717
and you just said it pretty much.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.586
You admitted what I said was right.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:00.987
They said he didn't have

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.789
the right to do it

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.290
and he did have the right to do it.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.192
And that's why they changed the law

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.794
taking that right away.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.095
I should note that your campaign paid

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.997
for a recount that happened in Wisconsin.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.198
It actually had more votes

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.500
for President Biden by the end of it.

